; Sagittarius - Hunter's Draw + Starfall, the first COMBINATION (.ai/combo-spells.md section 3, ComboCatalog).
;
; Never a level-up card and never in the spell catalog for anyone but Artemis. Everyone else makes it in the
; Ascension strip, from Hunter's Draw at level 8 down Hunter's Mark and Starfall at level 8 down Constellation
; (Player.TryFuse), and gets it whole: its copy carries the two parents frozen as they were at the fusion
; (SpellData.ComboParents), Sagittarius.Freeze rewrites the numbers below from the frozen Starfall and clears the
; table, and it never levels.
;
; ARTEMIS OPENS ON IT (.ai/second-half.md 3.4, F2; ComboDefinition.StartsFusedFor): made, at level 1 of the table
; below, and every card levels it to 8. She never held its parents, so her copy carries none
; (SpellData.ReadsOwnTable) and Player.FireSagittarius reads this table instead: the rain is a Starfall on these
; numbers - BaseDamage one star's hit, BaseCooldown the cloudburst, BaseProjectileCount the stars a cloudburst lets
; fall (the most archers it lights), BaseRange the rain's width, the AreaSize lines each star's burst (px) - and
; every arrow is Sagittarius.TableArrowShare (0.7) of a star's hit, scaled by the draw as always, loosed from a bow
; that levels with her (Hunter's Draw down Hunter's Mark at this spell's level: its pierce, reach, nock and size;
; Player.SagittariusTableBow). The lines between the stars are Constellation's from level 1: the archer's figure is
; the recipe, not a level.
;
; Its level 8 is the fused copy's numbers - Starfall's level 8 with Constellation: 22 a star, 8 stars every 0.68 s
; over a 270 px rain, +9 px a burst - as The Taking's level 8 is the copy anyone else fuses; the big level 8 is the
; parent's own shape (Constellation doubles Starfall's hit). Damage at the even levels, a star at the odd ones and at
; 8, the rain wider at 4 and 7, each burst bigger at 3, 5 and 7, the cadence at every even level: a line at every
; level (RegressionChecks.ValidateOpeners). A star of 5 at level 1 rather than 6 is the measured one: the default bot
; at minute 8 had it at level 3 doing 38% of her damage, where 6 made it 46% (the Dark Wizard's The Taking: 29% at
; level 2). .ai/second-half.md, "F2, built".
;
; ElementWeights are the two parents' base tags summed (Metal, Wind, Light). A fused copy carries the parents'
; CURRENT weights summed instead (ComboCatalog.SumWeights). The one kind of spell allowed three; never four.
